# Wire dependency injection

Grafana builds its backend graph with Google Wire.

- Provider sets and injectors live in `pkg/server/wire.go` and `pkg/server/bootstrap/wire/inject.go`. `wire.Build(...)` there is the injector. The `wireinject` build tag keeps those files out of the normal build.
- `make gen-go` runs Wire and writes `pkg/server/wire_gen.go` and `pkg/server/bootstrap/wire/wire_gen.go`. The command is defined in the root `Makefile` (`gen-go`).
- Do not hand-edit those generated files. Change the provider set or the constructor, then run `make gen-go`.
- A new service constructor belongs next to the service, in `pkg/services/<domain>/`, and takes interfaces from that package. Register it in the existing provider set instead of constructing it inside an HTTP handler.
- Wire fails the generation when the graph has a missing provider or a cycle. Fix the provider set. Do not stub the generated file to make it compile.
